---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';

const discord = 'https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt';
---
<Layout title="Multiplayer servers" description="Join the official TNK3 hub and choose EU or US, browse community servers, and read the official server rules.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Community / Multiplayer</p>
  <h1>Multiplayer servers</h1>
  <p class="intro">Join the official Towns &amp; Kingdoms 3 network through the hub, or browse public worlds run by other players.</p>
  <nav class="toc-inline" aria-label="Server guide sections">
    <a href="#joining">Official network</a>
    <a href="#public-servers">Public servers</a>
    <a href="#shared-worlds">Official rules</a>
    <a href="#connection-help">Connection help</a>
  </nav>

  <div class="prose">
    <section id="joining">
      <h2>Join the official network</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Launch <strong>Towns &amp; Kingdoms 3: Beyond the Forge</strong> using the pack version announced for the official servers.</li>
        <li>Choose <strong>Official Server</strong> on the Minecraft title screen to open <strong>Multiplayer</strong>, then join the official hub entry. If it is missing, check the official Discord for the current address.</li>
        <li>In the hub, choose <strong>EU</strong> or <strong>US</strong> to enter your regional world.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section id="public-servers">
      <h2>Browse public servers</h2>
      <p>Open <strong>Multiplayer</strong> and look for the BisectHosting public server list. Pick a community server from the list and check its required pack version and rules before joining.</p>
      <p>To start your own world, follow the <a href={href('guides/server-setup/')}>server setup guide</a>. BisectHosting also explains <a href="https://help.bisecthosting.com/hc/en-us/articles/40028209800987-How-to-Add-a-Modpack-Server-to-the-Public-Server-List" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how to list an eligible public server</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="shared-worlds">
      <h2>Official server rules</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No griefing or stealing.</strong> Ask before changing someone else’s build, taking items, or using their machines.</li>
        <li><strong>Be nice.</strong> Treat other players with respect in chat and in-game. Bring disputes to staff if you can’t resolve them together.</li>
        <li><strong>Work together.</strong> Coordinate with neighbours on shared resources, nearby builds, and large factories. Agree on how shared projects and supplies will be used.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="availability">
      <h2>Server status</h2>
      <p>Check the <a href={discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener">official Discord</a> for the current pack version, maintenance notices and help finding the hub.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="connection-help">
      <h2>When joining fails</h2>
      <p>Check that your client uses the server’s exact pack build. If you still can’t join, keep the full disconnect message and <code>logs/latest.log</code> for the server staff. The <a href={href('support/#logs')}>troubleshooting guide</a> shows where to find the log.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
